\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Example}
\title{The InstructGPT-style RLHF pipeline}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{rlhf}
\tag{post-training}

\p{One prompt passes successively through supervised tuning,
comparison-based reward modeling, and PPO in the InstructGPT-style RLHF
pipeline.}

\tikzfig{\begin{tikzpicture}[
  box/.style={draw, rounded corners=2pt, align=center, font=\small,
    text width=27mm, minimum height=10mm},
  flow/.style={-{Stealth[length=2mm]}, thick}
]
\node[box] (demo) at (0,1.35) {demonstration\\$(x,y^\star)$};
\node[box] (sft) at (4.0,1.35) {supervised\\policy $\pi_{\rm SFT}$};
\node[box] (pair) at (8.0,1.35) {comparison\\$y_B\succ y_A$};
\node[box] (rm) at (8.0,-1.25) {reward model\\$r_A=0.2,\ r_B=0.8$};
\node[box] (ppo) at (4.0,-1.25) {PPO reward\\$0.8-0.1\log 2$};
\node[box] (pol) at (0,-1.25) {updated\\policy};
\draw[flow] (demo) -- (sft);
\draw[flow] (sft) -- node[font=\scriptsize, fill=white] {sample} (pair);
\draw[flow] (pair) -- node[font=\scriptsize, fill=white] {fit} (rm);
\draw[flow] (rm) -- (ppo);
\draw[flow] (ppo) -- (pol);
\end{tikzpicture}}

\p{For the displayed illustrative prompt, suppose the comparison-trained
reward model scores the preferred response by #{0.8}. If the candidate
policy assigns it twice the probability assigned by the reference policy and
the declared KL coefficient is #{\beta=0.1}, its shaped scalar is
##{
  0.8-\beta\log\frac{\pi(y_B\mid x)}
                         {\pi_{\rm ref}(y_B\mid x)}
  =0.8-0.1\log 2\approx0.731.
}}

\p{The stage ordering is grounded in
\citet{Sections 3.1--3.5}{ouyang2022training}; the numbers are a schematic
calculation rather than reported InstructGPT hyperparameters. The diagram
records the interface used in that pipeline. Other RLHF systems may order or
replace the stages differently.}
